title: "Numerical Tools for Aircraft Engine Vibration Analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tabarelli
    given-names: Filippo
    affiliation: "University of Padova (Università degli Studi di Padova)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tabarelli-filippo/MasterThesis-Codes"
url: "https://thesis.unipd.it/handle/20.500.12608/107544"
abstract: >
  FE-based reduced order models for rotordynamic and aeroelastic analysis
  of aircraft engines. Includes a 1D shaft-line finite element model (MATLAB)
  for lateral vibration analysis of multi-disk rotor systems, and a Python
  framework for aeroelastic identification using Blade Tip Timing measurements.
  Developed as part of a Master's Thesis at the University of Padova.
keywords:
